  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0220, and it contains seven tables. The tables are:\n1. Product: This table stores information about the products sold by the company. It has columns for the product brand, click count, image link, price, product ID (primary key), product title, and product type.\n2. Address: This table stores information about the addresses of customers and the postal codes used in the database. It has columns for the city, postal code (primary key), and state.\n3. Customer: This table stores information about the customers who have placed orders with the company. It has columns for the customer ID (primary key), email, name, and phone number.\n4. Product_Description: This table stores information about the descriptions of the products sold by the company. It has columns for the description content, description ID (primary key), description type, and product ID (foreign key referencing the Product table).\n5. Tax_Rate: This table stores information about the tax rates for different postal codes. It has columns for the postal code (foreign key referencing the Address table), tax rate, tax rate ID (primary key), and tax rate type.\n6. Order: This table stores information about the orders placed by customers. It has columns for the customer ID (foreign key referencing the Customer table), order date, order ID (primary key), order price, payment method, postal code (foreign key referencing the Address table), shipping method, tax, and total price.\n7. Order_Detail: This table stores information about the details of the orders placed by customers. It has columns for the detail ID (primary key), order ID (foreign key referencing the Order table), product ID (foreign key referencing the Product table), quantity, and total price.\nThe primary keys for each table are highlighted in bold. The foreign keys are denoted by the word \"foreign\" followed by the name of the referenced table. The update and delete rules for each foreign key are also specified, such as CASCADE or RESTRICT. The indexes and constraints for each table are also listed.",
  "gold_question": "This is an e-commerce system used to manage product information, order information, as well as related tax and geographic location data. The system allows adding, editing, and deleting product information, including product title, type, brand, price, image link, and click count. Multiple descriptions can be added to each product, including description content and type.\n\nThe system also handles address management, including postal codes, states, and city information, enabling users to select addresses conveniently when placing orders. Tax rates are recorded based on different postal codes and regions to ensure accurate tax calculations.\n\nThe system records users’ order information, including order price, tax, total price, order date, customers’ personal information, address information, payment method, and shipping method. It keeps track of products and quantities in each order, supporting detailed query and management of orders.\n\nBy analyzing product click counts, the system helps identify user interests and behavior, providing data support for marketing strategies.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0220.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0220\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_brand` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `click_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `address` (\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`postal_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product_description` (\n  `description_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `description_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`description_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_description_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tax_rate` (\n  `tax_rate_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `tax_rate` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax_rate_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tax_rate_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tax_rate_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`postal_code`) REFERENCES `address` (`postal_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `order_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `shipping_method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tax` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`postal_code`) REFERENCES `address` (`postal_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_detail` (\n  `detail_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`detail_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
